BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 14\}`]
- [`B = \{-6, -2, 3, 8\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 2 \leq x \leq 13\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cap A \cap C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(B \cup A) \cup B \cup B \cap (((B \cup (B \cup C)) \cup C)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

